# Sitecore (Angular)

- **Data:** loaders in `src/content-sdk/loaders/` attached with `loaderResolver('<key>')`; locale via `getLanguage(context)`, path via `splitLocaleFromPath`, site via `getSiteName(context)`
- **Client:** single lazy singleton `getClient()` in `src/content-sdk/client/sitecore-client.ts`; never `new SitecoreClient(...)` elsewhere
- **Preview:** `getEditingPreviewData(context.csdkRequestData)` → `getPreview()` / `getDesignLibraryData()`; editing is Metadata mode only
- **Fields:** structural directives `*scText`, `*scRichText`, `*scImage`, `*scLink`, `*scRouterLink`; validate before render; `scTextEncode="false"` only for trusted content
- **Placeholders:** `<sc-placeholder [name]="..." [rendering]="...">`
- **Components:** standalone under `src/app/components/`, `fields` / `params` / `rendering` inputs, default export
- **Map:** `.sitecore/component-map.ts` generated from `src/app/components/`; provided via `SITECORE_COMPONENT_MAP`
- **Config:** change it only in `sitecore.config.ts` — structural settings (`angular.locales`, `angular.loadersCache`, `angular.linkPrefetch`, `multisite`, `redirects`, `personalize`) go in the **first argument** of `defineConfig`, secrets and endpoints come from env. `scConfig.*` is the resolved read-only result — never assign to it

